Dear Christophe,

Please find below the Korea YTD TOCA OUT overview (excluding CD change) reque=
sted by Jeffrey. Three vessels have left BV so far this year (one bulk carrie=
r, two gas carriers). No tankers have left. Please view this email in HTML fo=
rmat for the full table and assessment.

1. ATLANTIC LION (36036W), Bulk carrier, GT 109,731, Sinokor (sold to HMM), 2=
026-06-04, Change of ownership
2. SAEHAN SELINA / C GAS (36642F), LPG, GT 3,428, Saehan -> SJ Tanker, 2026-0=
3-18, Change of ownership; commercial/pricing
3. HONGKONG ENERGY (37071W), Liquefied gas carrier, GT 96,165, Sinokor, 2026-=
05-13, Sale/scrapping

Key point: our fees are well above KR's for small and mid-sized Korean owners=
. If the gap stays, more TOCA OUTs and lost newbuilding opportunities are exp=
ected.

Kind regards,
Sang-Jin

